      "html": "<div id=\"step-q128157\" class=\"step questionWidget\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 3</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-128157\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\"><p>Which of the following terms describe the shape above?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  Square </li><li> Trapezoid </li><li>  Rhombus </li></ol></div><table class=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-128157-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II only </td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-128157-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">III only </td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-128157-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and II only   </td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-128157-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and III only   </td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-128157-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II and III only   </td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-128157-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-128157-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>Let's now look at the terms one by one.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The given figure is a quadrilateral where all sides are congruent and all angles are right, so it is a square.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Since the quadrilateral has two pairs of opposite sides that are parallel to each other, not one pair, it is <strong>not</strong> a trapezoid. </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The quadrilateral is a parallelogram where all sides are congruent. So it is a rhombus.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Consequently, the given shape is described by terms I (square)  and III (rhombus).</p>\n</div></div>",
